# Operator identifiers stay out of git

These are not app runtime secrets. They still must not land in the public tree.

- Put them in gitignored `.env.ops` (copy `.env.ops.example`). Empty values only in the example file.
- Never commit a Neon project slug, a `linear.app/<workspace>/` URL, or a `/Users/<name>/` (or `/home/<name>/`) path.
- Docs, tests, comments, fixtures, and commit messages name the env var (`NEON_PROD_PROJECT`) or a ticket id (`BOTP-10`), not the private value.
- Do not re-introduce a leaked value as a regex or string to "prove it is gone." Scan for the shape instead (`scripts/ops-identifiers.ts`).

If you find one already committed, stop and say so. Deleting the line does not erase git history.
